---
import WebsiteLayout from "../layouts/WebsiteLayout.astro";
---

<WebsiteLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="Privacy information and data-handling practices for visitors to the ImRabo website."
  path="privacy/"
>
  <div class="space-y-12">
    <section class="border-b border-border bg-muted/30">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 md:px-10 md:py-20 lg:px-12">
        <p class="mb-5 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">
          LEGAL / PRIVACY
        </p>

        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-6xl">
          Privacy notice<span class="text-primary">.</span>
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Information about how visitor data may be collected, used, stored and
          shared when accessing ImRabo websites and resources.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-7 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-border bg-card px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground">
          <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-amber-500"></span>
          DRAFT — LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6 md:p-8">
        <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
          This page is a drafting framework, not a finalized privacy policy. The
          actual data practices, responsible legal entity, applicable
          jurisdictions and contact details must be verified before this notice
          is published as an operative policy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-10 px-6 md:px-10">
      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          1. Information collected
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Document the categories of information actually collected through the
          website and related services. Depending on the implementation, this
          may include server logs, device and browser information, analytics
          data, contact messages, cookies and information provided through
          third-party embeds.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Do not state that no personal information is collected until hosting
          configurations, analytics tools, forms and external integrations have
          been reviewed.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          2. Purpose and legal basis
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Explain why each category of information is processed, the relevant
          purpose and the applicable legal basis under the privacy laws
          governing the services and jurisdictions served.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          3. Cookies and analytics
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Identify cookies, local storage, analytics scripts and similar
          technologies used by the website. Explain their purposes and any
          available visitor controls where applicable.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          4. Third-party services
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          List hosting providers, analytics services, embedded content,
          communication tools and other third parties that receive or process
          visitor information. Include relevant provider privacy notices where
          appropriate.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          5. Data retention and security
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Specify retention periods or the criteria used to determine them.
          Describe the security measures actually implemented without making
          unsupported guarantees.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">6. Visitor rights</h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Describe the rights available to visitors under applicable law,
          including relevant procedures for access, correction, deletion,
          objection or other privacy requests where those rights apply.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          7. International data transfers
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Document whether personal information is transferred across national
          borders and identify the safeguards required under applicable law.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">
          8. Changes to this notice
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Explain how updates to this notice will be published and how visitors
          can identify the latest effective version.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground">9. Privacy contact</h2>

        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
          Provide a monitored privacy contact address and identify the
          responsible organization or person before publication.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl border-t border-border px-6 pt-8 md:px-10">
      <p class="text-xs leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        Publication checklist: verify actual data flows, hosting and analytics
        providers, cookie behavior, retention, applicable jurisdictions,
        responsible entity, contact information and effective date. Obtain
        appropriate legal review.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</WebsiteLayout>
